% Test cases for the speech generating device policy
% (speech_generating_devices.le): synthetic claims, one or two per criterion
% of LCD L33739 and per payment condition of Policy Article A52469, each
% stating only what its record shows. Findings are recorded as the
% speech-language pathologist's, the treating practitioner's or the
% Council's. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query, so
% "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and
% what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base speech_generating_devices cases includes these resources:
    speech_generating_devices.

the knowledge base speech_generating_devices cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a synthesized speech device with multiple access
% methods (E2510) after ALS: the SLP's evaluation with its six elements
% before the delivery, forwarded before the order, the four findings, an
% independent SLP, the order and the delivery.
scenario device_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the speech device.
    the HCPCS code of the speech device is "E2510".
    the speech device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-02-10.
    the speech language pathologist formally evaluated the communication abilities of Ann on 2026-01-10.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes current communication impairment.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes assessment of natural modes of communication.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes functional communication goals.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes rationale for the device selected.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes treatment plan with a training schedule.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes abilities to use the device.
    the written evaluation of Ann was forwarded to the treating practitioner on 2026-01-15.
    the speech language pathologist who evaluated Ann has no financial relationship with the supplier.
    the finding severe expressive speech impairment about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "dysarthria from amyotrophic lateral sclerosis".
    the finding natural communication insufficient about Ann is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding other treatments ruled out about Ann is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding device will benefit speech about Ann is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the order for the speech device is dated 2026-01-20.
    the order for the speech device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the speech device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the speech device includes order date.
    the order for the speech device includes description of the item.
    the order for the speech device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the speech device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the speech device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-01-21.
    the speech device was delivered on 2026-02-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the speech device.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% An eye tracking accessory (E2599) of that device, medically needed and
% documented in the SLP's evaluation, but the claim does not state the
% manufacturer, product name and number the Article requires.
scenario eye_tracker_unidentified is:
    claim 1 is for the eye tracker.
    the HCPCS code of the eye tracker is "E2599".
    the accessory type of the eye tracker is ocular tracking device.
    the eye tracker is an accessory of the speech device.
    the eye tracker is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-02-10.
    the finding tracking accessory medically needed about Ann is established, according to the speech language pathologist, because "the beneficiary has lost the use of both hands".
    the written evaluation of Ann documents the need for the eye tracker.
    claim 1 states the supplier price list amount of the eye tracker.
    the order for the eye tracker is dated 2026-01-20.
    the order for the eye tracker is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the eye tracker includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the eye tracker includes order date.
    the order for the eye tracker includes description of the item.
    the order for the eye tracker includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the eye tracker includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the eye tracker was communicated to the supplier on 2026-01-21.
    the eye tracker was delivered on 2026-02-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the eye tracker.
    the HCPCS code of the speech device is "E2510".
    the speech device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the speech language pathologist formally evaluated the communication abilities of Ann on 2026-01-10.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes current communication impairment.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes assessment of natural modes of communication.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes functional communication goals.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes rationale for the device selected.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes treatment plan with a training schedule.
    the written evaluation of Ann includes abilities to use the device.
    the written evaluation of Ann was forwarded to the treating practitioner on 2026-01-15.
    the speech language pathologist who evaluated Ann has no financial relationship with the supplier.
    the finding severe expressive speech impairment about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding natural communication insufficient about Ann is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding other treatments ruled out about Ann is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding device will benefit speech about Ann is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the order for the speech device is dated 2026-01-20.
    the speech device was delivered on 2026-02-10.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: claim 1 states the product identification of the eye tracker"]].

