    claim 1 is for the speech software.
    the HCPCS code of the speech software is "E2511".
    the speech software is furnished to Eve.
    Eve has another speech generating device.
    the speech language pathologist formally evaluated the communication abilities of Eve on 2026-01-10.
    the written evaluation of Eve includes current communication impairment.
    the written evaluation of Eve includes assessment of natural modes of communication.
    the written evaluation of Eve includes functional communication goals.
    the written evaluation of Eve includes rationale for the device selected.
    the written evaluation of Eve includes treatment plan with a training schedule.
    the written evaluation of Eve includes abilities to use the device.
    the written evaluation of Eve was forwarded to the treating practitioner on 2026-01-15.
    the speech language pathologist who evaluated Eve has no financial relationship with the supplier.
    the finding severe expressive speech impairment about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding natural communication insufficient about Eve is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding other treatments ruled out about Eve is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding device will benefit speech about Eve is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the order for the speech software is dated 2026-01-20.
    the speech software was delivered on 2026-02-10.
    rn expects answers [].

% Accessories of a covered E2508 device: a mounting system (E2512, claim 1)
% and an alternative input device for a beneficiary unable to use standard
% input (E2599, claim 2) are covered; an electromyographic sensor (E2513)
% is only for an E2510 (claim 3); a carrying case (E2599) is a convenience
% item (claim 4).
scenario accessories is:
    claim 1 is for the mount.
    the HCPCS code of the mount is "E2512".
    the mount is an accessory of the speech device.
    the mount is furnished to Fay.
    claim 2 is for the joystick.
    the HCPCS code of the joystick is "E2599".
    the accessory type of the joystick is alternative input device.
    the joystick is an accessory of the speech device.
    the joystick is furnished to Fay.
    claim 3 is for the sensor.
    the HCPCS code of the sensor is "E2513".
    the sensor is an accessory of the speech device.
    the sensor is furnished to Fay.
    claim 4 is for the carrying case.
    the HCPCS code of the carrying case is "E2599".
    the accessory type of the carrying case is carrying case.
    the carrying case is an accessory of the speech device.
    the carrying case is furnished to Fay.
    the finding standard input devices unusable about Fay is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding tracking accessory medically needed about Fay is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the HCPCS code of the speech device is "E2508".
    the speech device is furnished to Fay.
    the speech language pathologist formally evaluated the communication abilities of Fay on 2026-01-10.
    the written evaluation of Fay includes current communication impairment.
    the written evaluation of Fay includes assessment of natural modes of communication.
    the written evaluation of Fay includes functional communication goals.
    the written evaluation of Fay includes rationale for the device selected.
    the written evaluation of Fay includes treatment plan with a training schedule.
    the written evaluation of Fay includes abilities to use the device.
    the written evaluation of Fay was forwarded to the treating practitioner on 2026-01-15.
    the speech language pathologist who evaluated Fay has no financial relationship with the supplier.
    the finding severe expressive speech impairment about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding natural communication insufficient about Fay is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding other treatments ruled out about Fay is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding device will benefit speech about Fay is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the order for the speech device is dated 2026-01-20.
    the speech device was delivered on 2026-02-10.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The Council finds the record does not show that natural communication
% cannot meet the beneficiary's speaking needs: not reasonable and
% necessary.
scenario council_natural_communication_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the speech device.
    the HCPCS code of the speech device is "E2502".
    the speech device is furnished to Gus.
    the speech language pathologist formally evaluated the communication abilities of Gus on 2026-01-10.
    the written evaluation of Gus includes current communication impairment.
    the written evaluation of Gus includes assessment of natural modes of communication.
    the written evaluation of Gus includes functional communication goals.
    the written evaluation of Gus includes rationale for the device selected.
    the written evaluation of Gus includes treatment plan with a training schedule.
    the written evaluation of Gus includes abilities to use the device.
    the written evaluation of Gus was forwarded to the treating practitioner on 2026-01-15.
    the speech language pathologist who evaluated Gus has no financial relationship with the supplier.
    the finding severe expressive speech impairment about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding natural communication insufficient about Gus is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the evaluation records intelligible speech in short phrases and effective writing for longer messages".
    the finding other treatments ruled out about Gus is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the finding device will benefit speech about Gus is established, according to the speech language pathologist.
    the order for the speech device is dated 2026-01-20.
    the speech device was delivered on 2026-02-10.
    rn expects answers [].
